cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReviewHub in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ReviewHub: a local tool for scoping, systematic and rapid literature reviews"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Draheim
    given-names: Lukas
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/snova-digital/reviewhub"
abstract: >-
  ReviewHub supports the full workflow of a literature review on your own computer:
  protocol and eligibility framework (PCC, PICO, SPIDER, …), documented searches with
  imports from bibliographic databases, deduplication, independent title/abstract and
  full-text screening with calibration, inter-rater agreement (Cohen's kappa) and
  consensus, data charting and coding, critical appraisal, a live PRISMA flow diagram,
  evidence maps and co-occurrence networks. Human and LLM/agent reviewers work side by
  side; agent decisions are stored with a per-criterion reasoning log.
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - scoping review
  - PRISMA
  - JBI
  - screening
  - inter-rater agreement
  - evidence map
